{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits","id":1527711,"title":"Life sphere and stats limits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-01T14:45:14-08:00","id":1527711,"title":"Life sphere and stats limits","content":"Let's say your character posess the level 5 life sphere. He want to permanently transform his body to increase his physical limit, allowing him to buy a 6/7/8 dot and so on with xp.<br /> <br /> According to m20 it would require more than 20 success (let's say 26) with the level 5 of the sphere. Still according to the raw the basic difficulty would be 8 but the mage could set up a ritual to lower it to minimum 5 (-3).<br /> Final obstacle the mage can maintain a ritual for 1 hour per dot in stamina, after that he must roll to maintain the ritual.<br /> What prevent him from using level 3 of the spere to increase temporarly his stamina and increase his chance of success? And how many dot would he manage to get? 10 as the 3rd gen vampires? More?<br /> <br /> I only have the m20 book yet, is there any more detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T16:19:15-08:00","id":1527721,"title":"","content":"There really isn't a rule that lets Mages use Life to increase their ability to buy Attributes above 5. Mages can get Attributes to high levels, but it would always come with the risks of Permanent Paradox or Genetic Flaws as per the Enhancement Background. Using Life and performing a high level ritual to rewrite your pattern can only fend off the risk of Pattern Bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T16:49:38-08:00","id":1527723,"title":"","content":"Increasing Attributes above 5 is dangerous due to paradox, but I do think we should see more mages with increased attributes stats.<br /> <br /> I can see arguments that some mages won't increase their appearance, thinking it's vain and beneath them or that it just doesn't matter. I can even see arguments against increasing one's strength. I'm a wizard and a gentleman, physical labor is beneath me. Or magic can just do anything strength can do, but better.<br /> <br /> But everyone who can should increase their stamina and dexterity to 5. Stamina increases your survivability and casting can be quite strenuous. It helps everyone. Likewise, fine motor control can help with many different instruments and rituals, and if you're in even occasional combat, maxing out your dex can save your life.<br /> <br /> Then there's the mental stats, if you have the spheres for increasing them and your paradigm allows it, why would anyone not increase them all to 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T01:34:22-08:00","id":1527756,"title":"","content":"As pointed out in another thread, it's doable; but if you want to permanently boost your attributes to 5 without paying some sort of price such as those that Enhancements have, you need to take the appropriate time to properly integrate those increases into your Pattern \u2014 which, in game terms, means paying the necessary experience points, or something equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T13:21:54-08:00","id":1527783,"title":"","content":"I've read that the enhancement background is fixing the maximum permanent stats upgrade to 8 for genetic enginiring, so it answer my question on how many permanent dot you canb develop with a ritual, you could go beyond with magyc enchancement in addition but you would have to maintain the effect<br /> <br /> About that if a pc use a ritual to create a personal shield using the succes repartition to gain a permanent powerful invisible protection triggering at will he would be able do it these kind of benediction must be maintain on himself by increasing his other arete difficulty ? (I'm not sure if i'm clear, since mage is complex))<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T03:50:07-08:00","id":1527828,"title":"","content":"Um, yeah, I'm having a lot of trouble understanding you on that last post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T05:42:33-08:00","id":1527833,"title":"","content":"I think what they are asking is this.<br /> <br /> If a Mage casts a ritual to create a triggered personal force field(aka can be turned on and off at will), and then ties this effect to himself (all but permanent duration and tied to his own pattern), does this increase the difficulty for all other arete rolls he might make?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T06:33:32-08:00","id":1527837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furoan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527833#post1527833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what they are asking is this.<br /> <br /> If a Mage casts a ritual to create a triggered personal force field(aka can be turned on and off at will), and then ties this effect to himself (all but permanent duration and tied to his own pattern), does this increase the difficulty for all other arete rolls he might make?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's it, by using the Force sphere for the protection, life (i think) to tie it to your pattern and psyche to activate it at will (if my sphere combinaison is correct). Using a ritual and gain enough success to make it really resistant (around 10 dice for absorption, more or even indestructible if feasible with a higher sphere level or more success ) and permanent by using the optionnal rule to split success between the effect and it's duration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T08:20:56-08:00","id":1527840,"title":"","content":"Plus now that i think about it even if you have permanent shield, even resistant it could be broken by an attack that surpass it's absorption, it would need health to stay active in that case. So it would need the prime sphere to give it energy at least to exist in the first place (spend 1 quintessence when casting, but would it means that you need to allocate success as &quot;health&quot; of the shield or spend quintessence to create them, like 1 quintessence for 1 health point?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:25:57-08:00","id":1527861,"title":"","content":"Not an expert on the casting system of Mage, but my interpretations, in M20 rules, would be as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) If your shield is activated by thought, then it will contribute to the Difficulty penalty produced by active Effects; something that requires active management by the Mage requires &quot;concentration,&quot; while something running passively &quot;in the background&quot; won't.<br /> <br /> If your shield is just always running, and you gained sufficient successes for a limitless Duration, then it will not count as an active Effect; it won't add to the Difficulty penalty.<br /> <br /> I think that you could also avoid the penalty with the thought-activated shield using Life to &quot;lock&quot; it to your Pattern, but I'm a bit fuzzier on those rules.<br /> <br /> 2) Most forms of shields used by Mages don't have health pools, per se. They work by increasing the Difficulty of attacks, so attacks that are negated by the shield just don't get through. In more extreme cases, a Ward against the attack in question would just absolutely negate it, forget talking about Difficulty increases.<br /> <br /> 3) (Almost missed this one) You would not need to divide successes between Duration and &quot;shield power&quot; in M20 rules. Divided successes are (optionally) only used when you are combining Damage AND Duration together somehow. It's just a perk of the system that a lot of buff spells give you a better buff AND longer Duration at the same time when you get more successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:10:21-08:00","id":1527870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527861#post1527861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If your shield is activated by thought, then it will contribute to the Difficulty penalty produced by active Effects; something that requires active management by the Mage requires &quot;concentration,&quot; while something running passively &quot;in the background&quot; won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least when the shield is active in that case, not when you let him off, it seems logical to me<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527861#post1527861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your shield is just always running, and you gained sufficient successes for a limitless Duration, then it will not count as an active Effect; it won't add to the Difficulty penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case it would have side effect like preventing the mage from touching things and any contact with other being would be complicated unless he thought of it by making the spell more complex, maybe with Enthropy to make the shield recognise what is a threats and what's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527861#post1527861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you could also avoid the penalty with the thought-activated shield using Life to &quot;lock&quot; it to your Pattern, but I'm a bit fuzzier on those rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case i had in mind, a benediction to himself that warrior mage (or a cautious one) could use when he's fighting humans soldiers or more dangerous beings like raging Werewolves and Mad Brujah Vampires capable of Aggr Damages<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527861#post1527861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Most forms of shields used by Mages don't have health pools, per se. They work by increasing the Difficulty of attacks, so attacks that are negated by the shield just don't get through. In more extreme cases, a Ward against the attack in question would just absolutely negate it, forget talking about Difficulty increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>A shield built with correspondence that deviate attack or with time that make them slow them down would indeed increased attack difficulty but a force field would just let them crush on it so it would need strength to soak damage, no?<br /> By the way if you use a shield to increase attack difficulty, each success would make it rise by one up to 9 and then you ask 1 success to overcome per additional success? So Difficulty 6 against a shield built with 5 success would increase to difficulty 9 +2 success to overcome<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527861#post1527861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) (Almost missed this one) You would not need to divide successes between Duration and &quot;shield power&quot; in M20 rules. Divided successes are (optionally) only used when you are combining Damage AND Duration together somehow. It's just a perk of the system that a lot of buff spells give you a better buff AND longer Duration at the same time when you get more successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically if you have 6 success the shield increase the difficulty by 6 and is permanent at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 01-03-2024, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T14:25:50-08:00","id":1527880,"title":"","content":"Locking does indeed remove the difficulty penalty for active effects. It takes a Pattern Sphere at rank 2 to lock an effect to the appropriate pattern. M20 never directly says what sphere level you need, but every clear example uses 2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T08:29:43-08:00","id":1527924,"title":"","content":"After talking with a friends, we realised there's a lot of thing that could potentially let mage get a lot a permanent effect<br /> <br /> Life sphere create patern bleeding unless using level 5, but if you manage to use this level you could grant yourself eternal life, copying shapechanger ability to become a fake werewolf (without rage, gnosis and gift), regeneration and so on, and from what we read in the enhencement background, the genetic improvement does not cause permanent paradox unless visible.<br /> <br /> A smart mage could get growing et retractable wings, to hide it, or give himself the innatr ability to grow claws and fang instead of keeping them all the time.<br /> <br /> The clear limitation is the genetic flaws each mutation cause to the mage (listed at the end of the book before enchanted things). But can it be avoided by getting more success or is it to unpredictable? It is said these flaws are caused by the lack of knowledge of cellular fonctions but life sphere 1 can give the mage the perception to get it, no?<br /> <br /> The locked effects on the other hand does not cause genetic flaws, and if we understood correctly they do not cause paradox unless visible.<br /> <br /> For the shield exemple if you lock the effect on your pattern, set it invisible and use the enthropy spere to make it trigger automatically when the mage is in danger, it only cause temporary paradox when activated<br /> <br /> In that case you coud provide yourself multiple benediction like this to protect yourself, or even give yourself innate powers ability if you accept suffering genetic flaws","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T09:05:16-08:00","id":1527925,"title":"","content":"Genetic Flaws aren't caused by a lack of knowledge; they're caused by impatience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T10:00:36-08:00","id":1527929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527925#post1527925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genetic Flaws aren't caused by a lack of knowledge; they're caused by impatience.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they can be avoided by taking more time and success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:01:29-08:00","id":1527932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527924#post1527924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the shield exemple if you lock the effect on your pattern, set it invisible and use the enthropy spere to make it trigger automatically when the mage is in danger, it only cause temporary paradox when activated</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Mage Shield Effects tend to be Coincidental on their own, and Effects don't generate Paradox after they have been cast AFAIK, outside of extreme Storyteller Fiat situations perhaps.<br /> <br /> If a Mage is seen with a blatant and Vulgar Effect running, but it was previously cast in a Sanctum, etc., then it's not going to be Paradox that causes you problems, but Disbelief (that's not the right term, but I'm drawing a blank atm), which causes Vulgar magic to break down when it's observed too much by Sleepers. I think M20 left the rules for it pretty fuzzy, though.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if there is actually any value to having the shield switching off and on unless we're talking about a literal &quot;Force field.&quot; Matter can turn your suit into armor without altering its appearance. Correspondence can basically give you eyes in the back of your head. Entropy would make you look a bit like a 'Drunken Master' who always managed to dodge at the last second due to &quot;luck,&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> So, using the examples listed above:<br /> <br /> A &quot;Force field&quot; would be pretty Vulgar once people noticed it, and it would likely unravel under sustained scrutiny by Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Upgrading your suit with Matter would likely manage to get you through a few hits, but eventually it would begin to unravel if you pushed it too far.<br /> <br /> I think the Correspondence and Entropy examples are at least mostly safe. I'm not sure if there's a &quot;Domino Effect&quot; rule for Disbelief as well, where repeated unbelievable coincidences can push effects that would be Coincidental on their own into Vulgar territory; it may be that if you dodge too many attacks without even looking that your Correspondence defence might begin to unravel.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:15:50-08:00","id":1527935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527929#post1527929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they can be avoided by taking more time and success?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, yes, with \u201ctaking more time\u201d being handled by paying for the new features with experience points. The one other gotcha, though, is that if the mods you're trying to implement are obviously inhuman, you're effectively turning yourself into a Thaumavore and/or a Bygone; see <b>Gods and Monsters</b> for systems relating to beings who aren't fully compatible with the mundane world, and what happens to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T13:53:56-08:00","id":1527948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527935#post1527935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, yes, with \u201ctaking more time\u201d being handled by paying for the new features with experience points. The one other gotcha, though, is that if the mods you're trying to implement are obviously inhuman, you're effectively turning yourself into a Thaumavore and/or a Bygone; see <b>Gods and Monsters</b> for systems relating to beings who aren't fully compatible with the mundane world, and what happens to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got this one recently, quickly overlooked it but still trying to get the basic rules before looking for more.<br /> Still buy a supernatural improvement? Like buying the 6th dot of strength? Where does it end then? I can't imagin a mage getting 10+ permanent dot in strength with xp witout turning into a giant, there's a limit on how compressed your muscular mass can be to keep a human shape and height. Plus how much would cost something like wolverine regeneration? Aliens Acid blood? Spider web appendage? And how many mutation can you put on yourself? The biopart seems to tell twice your stamina, same for genetics modifications?<br /> And for the locked effect like protective shield that trigger at will, it can be permanent as a benediction but the book also say that permanent effect are enchanted and must be created the same (wich would mean a mage can turn hiself into a wonder himself). Which also ask how many benediction can you put on someone at the same time? Same for wonder, up to 5 dot of on or multiple effect depending on the higher sphere used?<br /> <br /> So much question O_O ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T14:27:07-08:00","id":1527951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527924#post1527924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The locked effects on the other hand does not cause genetic flaws, and if we understood correctly they do not cause paradox unless visible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> So, once a spell has been cast, it can't generate Paradox later.<br /> <br /> However, if you cast a spell that's vulgar without witnesses, it's still vulgar, and thus still generates paradox.<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, this is why Permanent Paradox is really a thing (esp. since it's not actually permanent). It exists to cover situations where you're in your Sanctum, the spell is coincidental, but when you leave, it would be considered vulgar (and again, remember that vulgar w/o witnesses is still vulgar), by having a form of lingering Paradox that hangs on your character. Permanent Paradox just doesn't actually &quot;do&quot; anything until you start causing more Paradox (I think this might be why you're thinking it doesn't &quot;create&quot; paradox unless &quot;visible&quot;).<br /> <br /> So, if you have a bunch of Permanent Paradox incurring spells on you, and you just walk around not doing anything magical, nothing happens... if you provoke Paradox, it gets bad scaled to how much Permanent Paradox you built up by adding dice to your Backlash pool that don't go away like normal Paradox dice after a backlash.<br /> <br /> So, there's basically a risk-reward to this method. You can have these powers one you, and then try to act subtly and not incur Paradox, and get away with a lot of buffs to your character... but that comes with a high risk of blowing up in your face when things get tense - even a simple coincidental spell risks botching and causing Paradox - and all that power finally kicks back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T14:34:13-08:00","id":1527954,"title":"","content":"I think you are confusing spells that have indefinite duration, effects that are permanent, and wonders.<br /> <br /> Spells with indefinite duration are active spells that will persist until they are ended. The spell is still there and can be unwoven if you are using those rules. Your locked protective shield is this kind of magic. <br /> <br /> That's not the same as a permanent change, where the magic is finished and the change to reality is set. In that case the spell already did its work and the effects it left behind are a perpetual part of reality.<br /> <br /> Finally, neither of those is a wonder, which is the ability to do sphere magic baked into an thing. A belt with a protective spell locked onto it is not a wonder. A belt that can cast a new protective spell on its wearer is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T14:59:20-08:00","id":1527958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527951#post1527951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, there's basically a risk-reward to this method. You can have these powers one you, and then try to act subtly and not incur Paradox, and get away with a lot of buffs to your character... but that comes with a high risk of blowing up in your face when things get tense - even a simple coincidental spell risks botching and causing Paradox - and all that power finally kicks back.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can set as many benediction on yourself as you want, the important part is to deal with the permanent paradox they cause (meaning that if there was no paradox mage would be really overpowered).<br /> <br /> So let's take 2 exemple of protection:<br /> The first one is a force field that protect you exactly like an armor would; bullets, fist and blade crush on it. In this case the spell is vulgar and if it's permanently locked on a mage he suffer permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> The second is an effect of the same sphere, force, but instead of creating a solid invisible wall it deviate slitly incoming attack. In that case it would be coincidental and would not cause paradox, unless every permanent effect cause paradox?<br /> <br /> Does the permanent paradox affect you if that permanent effect is set on another being? Let's say you put the force field on your human buddy to protect him from a threats, does it give the mage the permanent paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T23:43:37-08:00","id":1530873,"title":"","content":"Replying for the updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28202-karajoe","name":"KaraJoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T06:48:27-08:00","id":1530894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1527958#post1527958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you can set as many benediction on yourself as you want, the important part is to deal with the permanent paradox they cause (meaning that if there was no paradox mage would be really overpowered).<br /> <br /> So let's take 2 exemple of protection:<br /> <br /> The first one is a force field that protect you exactly like an armor would; bullets, fist and blade crush on it. In this case the spell is vulgar and if it's permanently locked on a mage he suffer permanent paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this doesn't cause permanent paradox. Even assuming the force field is extremely unnatural and attention grabbing (and therefore definitely vulgar) and that it is locked to the mage, this is not a source of permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> Locking is the metaphysical equivalent of duct taping a spell to something. It doesn't change the pattern the spell is locked to. If the spell is dispelled, the anchor pattern is completely unaffected. Normal paradox rules apply.<br /> <br /> Permanent Paradox happens when the mage's pattern itself is an affront to reality. That's why it is generally the result of Life enhancements, because that's what's necessary to change a pattern to that degree. If the mage rewrote his pattern so that he had an innate ability to breathe fire or generate force fields (which is harder than just locking) that might cause Perma-dox.<br /> <br /> To summarize: permanent spells don't cause permanent paradox. Having a pattern that reality hates causes permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the permanent paradox affect you if that permanent effect is set on another being? Let's say you put the force field on your human buddy to protect him from a threats, does it give the mage the permanent paradox? </div> </div> </div>Again, the force field wouldn't result in permanent paradox at all, but if you made your buddy into a fire breathing dragon he would get permanent paradox. Bygones (legendary creatures that no longer fit into reality) suffer from permanent paradox, so we know that it rests on the pattern that violates reality, not the one who created that pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T03:16:28-08:00","id":1530963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1530894#post1530894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, this doesn't cause permanent paradox. Even assuming the force field is extremely unnatural and attention grabbing (and therefore definitely vulgar) and that it is locked to the mage, this is not a source of permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> Locking is the metaphysical equivalent of duct taping a spell to something. It doesn't change the pattern the spell is locked to. If the spell is dispelled, the anchor pattern is completely unaffected. Normal paradox rules apply.<br /> <br /> Permanent Paradox happens when the mage's pattern itself is an affront to reality. That's why it is generally the result of Life enhancements, because that's what's necessary to change a pattern to that degree. If the mage rewrote his pattern so that he had an innate ability to breathe fire or generate force fields (which is harder than just locking) that might cause Perma-dox.<br /> <br /> To summarize: permanent spells don't cause permanent paradox. Having a pattern that reality hates causes permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, the force field wouldn't result in permanent paradox at all, but if you made your buddy into a fire breathing dragon he would get permanent paradox. Bygones (legendary creatures that no longer fit into reality) suffer from permanent paradox, so we know that it rests on the pattern that violates reality, not the one who created that pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's perfetcly clear, thanks a lot. And ut appear that without paradox mage would be extremely powerful. By the way Life 5 can rewrite permanently patterns if the mage get at least 20 success and will avoid pattern bleeding, right? My translated book say this level allow permanent change and in the same time say in the reference success grid that it require 20 success. A bit confusing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T04:47:46-08:00","id":1530969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1530963#post1530963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that's perfetcly clear, thanks a lot. And ut appear that without paradox mage would be extremely powerful. By the way Life 5 can rewrite permanently patterns if the mage get at least 20 success and will avoid pattern bleeding, right? My translated book say this level allow permanent change and in the same time say in the reference success grid that it require 20 success. A bit confusing</div> </div> </div> </div>In case it helps revised has the permanent rewriting to be life 4 at least for upgrading attributes. Yes you avoid pattern bleeding. Also in revised you payed only half the normal xp cost to get it but i do not recommend this reduction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T11:22:40-08:00","id":1530993,"title":"","content":"This is one of those areas I think slipped through editing.<br /> <br /> Life 5 says it is the rank for permanent changes.<br /> <br /> Life 3/4 can enhance attributes or make significant but not drastic changes and by the rules they should be permanent changes with enough successes (and it should be significantly less than 20).<br /> <br /> HDYDT backs up the second option, not the first.<br /> <br /> You could just choose one or the other option, but if you want to try to reconcile the two here is one potential way: Life 3/4 effects can be made permanent by making the magic permanent. Life 5 effects can be made permanent by making the change permanent.<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is that a permanent Life 3/4 spell is an ongoing spell. It will last forever but if it does ever end the target reverts to their normal pattern (although they keep anything they've paid experience for). Because it is a spell it is vulnerable to unweaving, which can be done at lower ranks. As a permanent spell it uses the basic rules for any permanent spell: successes for the effect plus 6+ more successes for permanent duration.<br /> <br /> The Life 5 spell, though, isn't a permanent spell, it is an instantaneous spell that gives the target a new permanent pattern that is theirs forever. There is no unweaving this one because there's nothing to unweave. The only way to return someone to their original form is to cast a new spell. The duration rules apply to the duration of the spell and this one is practically instantaneous, so the caster doesn't need to spend successes for increased duration. On the other hand indelible changes to reality are much greater feats than ones propped up by an existing spell, so this is a significantly harder spell.<br /> <br /> Both can change the target's pattern to something rejected by reality so both of them can cause Permanent Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T11:50:55-08:00","id":1530995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1530993#post1530993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Life 3/4 can enhance attributes or make significant but not drastic changes and by the rules they should be permanent changes with enough successes (and it should be significantly less than 20).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tricky, considering that M20 p.502 says that rewrite your own pattern permanently need at least 20 success, either it mean that it's harder to change your own (wich i could understand) or there's an inconsistency. Considering that permanent change give you permanent paradox we could say it's up to the pc to choose his risks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T12:05:33-08:00","id":1530997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1530995#post1530995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tricky, considering that M20 p.502 says that rewrite your own pattern permanently need at least 20 success, either it mean that it's harder to change your own (wich i could understand) or there's an inconsistency. Considering that permanent change give you permanent paradox we could say it's up to the pc to choose his risks</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that what I am saying here is an optional attempt at reconciling the rules, not an official ruling.<br /> <br /> The Life 3/4 change is not a permanent change. It is a temporary change that lasts as long as the spell does. You pay successes to make the spell permanent.<br /> <br /> The Life 5 change is a permanent change that does not need an ongoing spell to keep it in place. You pay successes to create a new and perpetual reality. <br /> <br /> The Life 3/4 spells are cheaper, but subject to unweaving and unbelief. The Life 5 spells are more expensive, but can't be unwoven or disbelieved. Both can create ongoing patterns that violate the consensus, though, so both can cost permanent paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T16:59:46-08:00","id":1531011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1530997#post1530997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that what I am saying here is an optional attempt at reconciling the rules, not an official ruling.<br /> <br /> The Life 3/4 change is not a permanent change. It is a temporary change that lasts as long as the spell does. You pay successes to make the spell permanent.<br /> <br /> The Life 5 change is a permanent change that does not need an ongoing spell to keep it in place. You pay successes to create a new and perpetual reality.<br /> <br /> The Life 3/4 spells are cheaper, but subject to unweaving and unbelief. The Life 5 spells are more expensive, but can't be unwoven or disbelieved. Both can create ongoing patterns that violate the consensus, though, so both can cost permanent paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood, that attempt is smart, it will be useful.<br /> A friend pc asked what happen if he use life 5 to obtain more than five dots in his physical attributes, aside permanent paradox. The short answer is that his body will grow inhumaly big if he gain muscles, heavy if he touch stamina and so on, but just in case would you let him gain those stats with just the paradox or would you use that kind of side effect in addition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:36:52-08:00","id":1531110,"title":"","content":"That's largely dependent on the kind of game you want to run. By default, I think the choice is permanent paradox or flaws, so you don't have to add side effects at all if you don't want to. <br /> <br /> If you do decide to have additional effects they will likely depend on the paradigm and practices of the mage casting the spell. The genetic flaws section of M20 has a variety of possible side effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:46:03-08:00","id":1531111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531011#post1531011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understood, that attempt is smart, it will be useful.<br /> A friend pc asked what happen if he use life 5 to obtain more than five dots in his physical attributes, aside permanent paradox. The short answer is that his body will grow inhumaly big if he gain muscles, heavy if he touch stamina and so on, but just in case would you let him gain those stats with just the paradox or would you use that kind of side effect in addition?</div> </div> </div> </div>This definitely sounds like Genetic Flaws or the equivalent. And if the result is too radical (Storyteller's discretion), some Permanent Paradox <i>on top of that </i>might be warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T10:29:19-08:00","id":1531128,"title":"","content":"To prevent pc from getting too much advantage it seems fair to me, a mage giving hismelf regeneration and lethal + aggravated natural permanent soaking would give 2 or 3 permanent paradox and those 2 are already very powerfull for them. Adding a bit of side effect can give them another reason to think before get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T19:52:33-08:00","id":1531169,"title":"","content":"Someone, especially a mortal-mage, to have a strength of five, would look like Arnold Schwarzenegger from Conan the Barbarian, only a mage. Having a strength of six, isn't that much of a stretch; besides, it's not as heavy as it looked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T02:31:00-08:00","id":1531180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531169#post1531169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone, especially a mortal-mage, to have a strength of five, would look like Arnold Schwarzenegger from Conan the Barbarian, only a mage. Having a strength of six, isn't that much of a stretch; besides, it's not as heavy as it looked.</div> </div> </div> </div>A strength of 6 ok, but 8 or 10 i'ts going to be difficult to hide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T07:04:56-08:00","id":1531194,"title":"","content":"What it looks like will probably depend on the style of magic, and only some would have purely physical effects like bulking up or abnormal popping veins. A Verbena might use a variant of the mythological warp spasm and emit great amounts of heat after great exertion. An Adept might setStrength:= 7, and not change appearance at all, but their heavy lifting gets an unnatural &quot;floaty&quot; effect. A Chorister might summon angels and those who are looking see an aura surrounding the mage when he lifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T16:41:13-08:00","id":1531320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531194#post1531194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it looks like will probably depend on the style of magic, and only some would have purely physical effects like bulking up or abnormal popping veins. A Verbena might use a variant of the mythological warp spasm and emit great amounts of heat after great exertion. An Adept might setStrength:= 7, and not change appearance at all, but their heavy lifting gets an unnatural &quot;floaty&quot; effect. A Chorister might summon angels and those who are looking see an aura surrounding the mage when he lifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>With life sphere only? Or maybe with a mixed effect with force to get telekynesic effect (like an invisible exosuit)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T19:06:29-08:00","id":1531330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531320#post1531320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With life sphere only? Or maybe with a mixed effect with force to get telekynesic effect (like an invisible exosuit)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life is the sphere you need to increase the actual strength attribute. It\u2019s the method that changes the actual pattern, that accrues Permanent Paradox, and that shows uncanny side effects. But just because it is a Life effect doesn\u2019t mean that the side effects need to look biological. The side effects are happening in part because the body violates reality, they can violate expectations too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T19:14:35-08:00","id":1531331,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that is the changes make the character look sufficiently unnatural, there will likely be consequences for that. Permanent Paradox is one possibility; becoming a Thaumavore or even a Bygone is another, of the change is sufficiently radical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T08:30:32-08:00","id":1531359,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, when I was initially making a list of Traditions strength augment methods I did think of an invisible etherite exosuit. I discarded that because while it sounds so much more like a locked Forces spell. Don't get me wrong, it probably could be the practice for a Life augment, it just doesn't sound right so it makes for a confusing example","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T13:11:53-08:00","id":1531377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531330#post1531330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life is the sphere you need to increase the actual strength attribute. It\u2019s the method that changes the actual pattern, that accrues Permanent Paradox, and that shows uncanny side effects. But just because it is a Life effect doesn\u2019t mean that the side effects need to look biological. The side effects are happening in part because the body violates reality, they can violate expectations too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh i was focused on the biological part only, not the supernatural manifestation out of the body that could occure, interesting point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, when I was initially making a list of Traditions strength augment methods I did think of an invisible etherite exosuit. I discarded that because while it sounds so much more like a locked Forces spell. Don't get me wrong, it probably could be the practice for a Life augment, it just doesn't sound right so it makes for a confusing example</div> </div> </div> </div>This case raise the question of how strong, or precisely how many dots that invisible exosuit would provide beyond your actual level or even beyond 5. Considering it does not impact your pattern directly because it's a locked effect, a mage with lot of time and the good tool for a ritual could get a lot of dots. <br /> That lead to the question of how many paradox it would give you (i don't know why but the idea of 1 per dot obtained stick in my mind), would it have other side effect and how many success to get each dot since HDYDT as given a rule as 2 succes for each dot beyond five","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T14:05:54-08:00","id":1531380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527711-life-sphere-and-stats-limits?p=1531377#post1531377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This case raise the question of how strong, or precisely how many dots that invisible exosuit would provide beyond your actual level or even beyond 5. Considering it does not impact your pattern directly because it's a locked effect, a mage with lot of time and the good tool for a ritual could get a lot of dots.<br /> That lead to the question of how many paradox it would give you (i don't know why but the idea of 1 per dot obtained stick in my mind), would it have other side effect and how many success to get each dot since HDYDT as given a rule as 2 succes for each dot beyond five</div> </div> </div> </div>The exosuit (Forces 2/Life 2 should be good for the equivalent of any strength raises, at Forces 3 and beyond the character can pick up tanks) would use the standard paradox rules. In a sanctum it would be coincidental and therefore paradox free (or 2 points on a botch because of Forces 2). If its vulgar it would be one point of Paradox (3 on a botch without witnesses, 6 on a botch with witnesses). The power of the spell doesn't change much about the Paradox points accrued.<br /> <br /> There's a different force in place for handling spells that are already active: Unbelief. People's disbelief tends to wear away at the really flashy stuff. The more unbelievable it is, and the more people see it, the faster it degrades. This will manifest as paradigm appropriate failures that end the spell early. If the exosuit mage is juggling cars in Times Square it is likely his suit will have an overload or power failure and stop working until he can repair it (i.e. cast the spell again).<br /> <br /> There's no real system to this, so my recommendation is don't use this to limit how powerful the characters can get, use it to limit how powerful they can be in front of the sleepers. That exosuit mage could probably get several scenes of playing as Iron Man, even in a hostile reality zone, but in front of a crowd of witnesses he might get a handful of turns.<br /> <br /> I don't know how fast the life spell accrues permanent paradox, but I wouldn't start passing that out until the characters are getting above 5 in an attribute. If a normal sleeper can have the attribute, it doesn't violate reality enough for permanent paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-04-2024, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}